WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.571
SPEAKER: Today, I am going to
talk about Auto-Healing Managed

00:00:02.571 --> 00:00:03.590
Instance Groups.

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.070
Occasionally, a
bug or other error

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.444
might cause one
of your instances

00:00:06.444 --> 00:00:08.234
to get into a bad state.

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:09.650
With Auto-Healing
Instance Groups,

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.040
VMs that aren't
functioning correctly

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.010
are detected and recreated
so that you always

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.357
have the correct number
of healthy instances.

00:00:15.357 --> 00:00:16.940
I have an instance
group set-up, and I

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.110
want to add a health check to
it so I can use Auto-Healing.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.740
I click on the
instant group name,

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.119
and then I click Edit group.

00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:26.410
Now, I scroll down to the
Auto-Healing and Health Check

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:27.950
section.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.360
I create a New Health check.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.290
I give it a name.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:36.550
I'm going to check on Port 80
with HTTP on the base path.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.150
I want to check
every 60 seconds.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.540
And if there are three
unhealthy checks in a row,

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.100
I want to recreate the instance.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.450
Now, I click Save and
Continue, and click Save.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.770
And that's it.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.090
My managed instance group
is Auto-Healing now.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.800
I hope you found this
Cloud Minute helpful.

